{
 "what": "BWD-NEXT's placement on the tree after's unit (run_place.sh): membw.c -- read and copy bandwidth over a buffer of N MiB, each thread its own slice, the best of five (copy and copy-nt count the read and the write); tr_place.c -- the unit's own transposed product dV = P^T dY (att512_transposed, d = 32) and context product (att512_context) over one head's T2048 x T2048 P, the unit #included so its static kernels run as the backward runs them, and variant_tr.py's copies of it (BCIR_ATT_BAND 16 or 32 rows, a prefetch of P's lines PFD floats ahead with hint T0/T1/T2: b32p128T1 = band 32, 128 floats, T1); band_place.c -- the same products with P in 16-row bands: its own btr and bctx (the unit's register blocks and term order reading P through the band address), 'bp' the unit's att512_btransposed, and btr after every line of P written again (rewrite1) or the bands' lower parts (rewrite2); every result's bits checked against the unit's row walk on buffer 0 (tr_place prints a check sum); P resident (1 buffer, reused) or 16 buffers of 16 MiB in turn (256 MiB: the DRAM rate of membw's curve); TSC cycles a probability, the median of the calls; eight interleaved passes, one process a configuration; v1's rate 1.443",
